From d2965749a040843e4ad1e8558af419913f97d140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:33:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Tests: app-funded leases on the local verifier end to end;
 two test-environment fixes

test/lease-gas-verifier.e2e.test.mjs (reth --dev, the REAL verifier runtime, the real reserve/executor, the REAL relay
service, the real lease client given ONLY the verifier's client): the host's lease reads are one local-verifier authority;
an app-funded claim lands through the relay and is verified by the verifier (charged once); with the relay's answer lost
after landing, the lease is posted exactly once and a restarted client resolves its journal as landed from the chain;
with no proof source the claim refuses before anything is signed or posted, and resumes after. Helpers:
test/helpers/verifier-runtime.mjs (the runtime launcher, shared with the consumer E2E) and lease-gas-world.mjs
startWorldOn (the same world on an existing reth chain: funding by transfer, no anvil calls).
test/helpers/supervisor-wallet-fixture.mjs: its sliced supervisor context gets chainActionGate (a no-op, as in legacy
mode); without it the sliced sendLeaseTx threw and the real-lease-client cases failed.
test/owner-nomination.test.mjs: "a state file that cannot be written" used a 0500 directory, which root writes into (the
queued runner runs suites as root in a user namespace): the case failed identically on the 673601e54 baseline. The state
path's parent is now a regular file (ENOTDIR for any user); the assertions are unchanged.
